---
import LegalPage from '../components/legal/LegalPage.astro'
import { site } from '../lib/site'
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How Steelyard collects, uses and protects personal data, and the rights you have under the GDPR."
  lastUpdated="2026-10-03"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what personal data Steelyard collects, why, and what
    rights you have. It covers this website, the Steelyard application, and the
    data our customers bring into it.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    For this website, demo requests and customer accounts, Steelyard is the{' '}
    <strong>controller</strong>. For the spend data a customer imports from its
    ERP (invoices, invoice lines, suppliers and uploaded agreements), the
    customer is the controller and Steelyard is its <strong>processor</strong>,
    acting only on the customer's instructions under a data processing
    agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Demo requests:</strong> your name, work email, company, company
      size, your message, and the time you gave consent.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Accounts:</strong> name, email address, organization and role,
      used to sign you in and manage access.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Spend data:</strong> invoices, invoice lines, supplier details and
      agreements imported from the customer's ERP or uploaded by the customer.
      These can include names of supplier contacts.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical data:</strong> IP address and browser details, used for
      security and to prevent abuse.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why we use it, and on what basis</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To answer a demo request and book a meeting, based on your consent.</li>
    <li>
      To provide the service to customers, based on our contract with them.
    </li>
    <li>
      To keep the service secure and prevent abuse, based on our legitimate
      interest.
    </li>
    <li>To meet legal obligations such as bookkeeping rules.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal data, and we do not use customer data to train AI
    models for anyone else.
  </p>

  <h2>Where data is stored</h2>
  <p>
    Data is hosted in the European Union. We use a small number of
    sub-processors for hosting, sign-in and AI inference. Each is bound by a
    data processing agreement, and we will tell customers before adding a new
    one.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Demo requests are kept for 24 months, then deleted.</li>
    <li>
      Customer data is kept while the customer uses Steelyard. When a company is
      removed, its data is deleted.
    </li>
    <li>
      Security logs are kept for as long as needed to investigate incidents.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This website does not use tracking or advertising cookies. It remembers your
    light or dark theme in your browser, and that choice never leaves your
    device.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask to access, correct or delete your personal data, to restrict or
    object to its use, to receive it in a portable format, and to withdraw
    consent at any time. If your data is in Steelyard because your employer is a
    customer, we will pass your request on to them. You can also complain to
    your national data protection authority; in Denmark, that is Datatilsynet.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.privacyEmail}`}>{site.privacyEmail}</a>{' '}
    with any question about this policy or your data.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
